## SEVERITY / VERDICT
*Blocker:* a path beyond the one; a product byte; a diff line beyond the shape of Check 1 or a changed old pair; a cell added, lost or renamed; the head moved (C-68); the HEAD file green under M1 (the rows do not pin the arm) or the BASE file RED under M1 (the gap is not what the ticket says); a new key dead under its own per-key mutant; the counts blob other than main's; the verify pair other than 5170/307 or a red inside the rd774 file; a person name, decision-card id or secret in the message; a NEW CodeQL alert (any level the ruleset's thresholds name) on the changed lines. *Major (class named on the line, "NO GO 1 of 2"):* a new key that is red under its mutant for a reason other than the arm (for example M4 reddening a new key); a builder claim contradicted by your measurement that changes the basis (for example M1 on the head reds only 2 of 3 keys); a red outside the file at the verify that you cannot show is a port-band collision unrelated to the branch. *Minor/Note:* the zero-limit finding (report it, no key); M3 erroring rather than comparing counts (the builder said so; record what you see); the head `unsigned`; branch name carries the builder tag; node differing from CI; CodeQL PENDING at the verdict; the HTTP shape of the same arm not held by any cell; the comment wording. **VERDICT RULES.** GO needs Checks 1-6 measured with their controls, every pair equal, and CI/CodeQL read LAST with every `Analyze (<language>)` run completed and the PR's open alerts zero (control fired); if any analysis is pending or the node/CI parity is open, the best token is GO WITH FINDINGS with the open item named on the line above the last line (never a bare GO when CodeQL was not complete); a NO GO names the class and "round 1 of 2" and gives the fix-shape in prose. **STOP (`STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <the change and why>`) if** the delta holds a path beyond the one, the head moved, main moved into a path listed in Check 6, a request leaves loopback from your own scripts (other than GitHub GETs, npm as `npm ci` itself reaches it, `git fetch`), a system dialog blocks, or a security-shaped finding you cannot classify.
